WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Astronauts show higher hip fracture rates after space flights longer than 90 days than after shorter missions. This is Planetterrian Daily, Episode 200, Episode 200. Thanks for sticking with us. A study in Mayo Clinic Proceedings surveyed U.S. astronauts using Bayesian probabilistic modeling of fracture reports from annual exams. Gene D. Sabonga at NASA Johnson Space Center led the work titled, Increased Rates of Hip Fractures associated with

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.060
longer spaceflight durations. Matthew T. Drake of Hospital for Special Surgery co-authored

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:42.360
the editorial, Bone Loss in Astronauts. NASA plans multiple missions longer than six months,

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:49.520
including Artemis IV in 2028. Bone adapts to sustained low mechanical loading via osteosite

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:55.020
signaling. The same principle applies to prolonged bedrest or reduced mobility on Earth.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:01.220
Now, shifting to stem cell work, a career research institute of bioscience and biotechnology

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:07.800
team, led by Saun Mi Young and Lee Mi Ok, published in Experimental and Molecular Medicine.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:17.280
Application of Swingozine 1 Phosphate, or the S1PR1 selective agonist SEW2871 to human

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.640
pleuripotent stem cells, yielded more than 90% differentiation into cardiomyocytes.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:28.640
The cardiomyocytes showed increased cell size, densely aligned sarcominers, and more

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:29.940
regular pacing signals.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:35.560
Bovine serum is avoided because the specific component responsible for growth was unknown

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:36.660
until this work.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:43.740
Mature cardiomyocytes transplanted into animals with myocardial infarction and grafted into cardiac

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.220
tissue.

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.560
From mechanical loading signals in bone to molecular signals that guide stem cell maturation in the heart,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:55.560
A new naturopaper links erosion of cellular identity to aging processes.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:59.380
The study connects to ongoing discussions and ground truths.

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:06.060
Researchers examine which epigenetic information is lost during aging, from epigenetic stability

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:09.660
inside cells to the proteins that maintain gene silencing.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.480
A protein essential for compacting genes and turning off unnecessary genes requires a

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.900
to reach its site.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:19.900
Mutation of this protein links to cancer.

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:22.840
Researchers identified the delivery mechanism

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:25.060
that keeps genes bound and inactive,

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.300
from nuclear protein trafficking

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:29.920
to another scalable biotechnology tool.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.440
PushMeetColy and colleagues

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:34.940
at Google DeepMond developed a method

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.420
to watermark AI-generated proteins.

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.060
The approach maintains protein function

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.820
while establishing provenance.

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:43.660
The work appears in nature.

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:50.780
From design proteins to designed microbial metabolism in food, D-T-U National Food Institute

00:02:50.780 --> 00:02:56.600
and R-Hoo's University researchers showed microorganisms can change amino acid profiles

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.640
in plant foods.

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:02.060
The modification makes the foods more nutritious for humans and animals.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.560
Specific microbial action targets amino acid balance rather than broad fermentation.

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:14.500
From food composition to everyday physical capacity, Grayson Wickham recommends 2-4 short

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:17.120
sets of grip work 2-4 days per week.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:23.400
Each set involves squeezing as hard as possible for 5-10 seconds or 10-20 controlled reps.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.900
Free weights such as dumbbells, barbells, and kettlebells train support grip needed for

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:29.820
everyday items.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:35.420
Farmer carries with dumbbells or kettlebells held for 20-40 seconds before grip fatigue

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:36.900
build the same capacity.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:42.080
Wickham advises stopping one to two reps before failure to protect tendons.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:49.120
From maintaining physical resilience to population-level longevity patterns, Rougau in Jiangsu Province

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:53.500
records an average life expectancy of 83.12 years.

00:03:54.140 --> 00:03:59.140
105-year-old Gao Tinkuan rises at 5 a.m. to buy groceries and cook.

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:06.780
96-year-old Zhang Mingde washes dishes, waters, flowers, and piety daily. Nobel laureate Michael

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:12.660
Levitt stated that health-span determinants include eating well, not drinking too much, not smoking,

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:19.800
spending time in nature, exercising, and having friends. Levitt spoke at the 2026 collaborative

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:25.160
innovation conference on disease prevention research and translational achievements. From

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:30.980
From observed longevity to the cellular mechanism still under study, Professor Huimen Zhao of

00:04:30.980 --> 00:04:36.220
the University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign spoke at the Korean Society for Biotechnology

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:38.320
2026 Fall Meeting.

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:45.360
He leads the NSF Global Center for Bio-Foundary Applications and heads the NSF AI Institute

00:04:45.360 --> 00:04:46.700
for Molecular Synthesis.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:53.420
Zhao operates eye-bio-foundry where experiments are designed in natural language and AI directs

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:53.720
robots.

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:59.180
He noted that fixed workflows have limits because each user wants different experiments.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.900
AI allows students to converse with the system to design and check experiment feasibility.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.680
Korea has focused on workflow development in past proposals with less emphasis on AI.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:17.200
Every fall, monarchs fuel on nectar from Iowa fall blooming wildflowers before traveling to Mexico.

00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:22.800
Researchers note that pathways and effects of weather on travel remain largely unknown.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:27.640
new tracking aims to fill gaps in understanding how environmental factors shape

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:33.000
the root. Modified medication in a nature-reported study targets cells that form

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.400
endometriosis lesions. The approach shows early promise for the condition

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:42.900
affecting 190 million people. The skull bone marrow acts as a source of cells

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.200
that induce brain inflammation after injury. Fental Fibrate, a PPAR alpha

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:53.700
agonist may mitigate this response. The paper appears in science translational medicine.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:06:03.360
In 862 women, spine bone density fell 10.6% over 10 years, with 7.4% lost in the three-year window.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:11.660
Femre density fell 9.1% with 5.8% lost in the same period. The window runs from one year before

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:17.440
to two years after the final menstrual period. UK scientists developed a floating scarecrow

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.540
and repurposed a bird-scaring kite.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.480
Trials showed reduced entanglement of threatened sea birds.

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:26.840
The method offers a practical tool for fisheries.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:33.540
Next time, keep an eye on further details from the KRIBB stem cell maturation work as

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.540
additional cell lines undergo testing.

